      "writtenOn": "2017-12-16T01:39:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My mistake; I messed that up.\n\nBut, that is a good question. I think the answer would be no. A device that has volume buttons shouldn\u0027t need a dedicated recovery button as the volume button combination can be used to request recovery. It\u0027d save a pin too.\n\nFor confirmation, I think that other keyboard-less devices use the power button.\n\nThough, now that I think about it, why don\u0027t devices like fizz use the power button for confirmation? Maybe because there\u0027s already a separate recovery button, so we might as well use it?",
      "parentUuid": "4942c178_705e462a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 737,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 737,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "d74115262d8693fd8dbc556b553e91c7eed84d36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6155cdb8_20ef3cf6",
        "filename": "common/button.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 737,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-12-17T22:59:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e why don\u0027t devices like fizz use the power button for confirmation? \n\nI think power button press is supposed to shut down the system immediately on firmware screens. I fixed a bug for Fizz not doing so. So, there is a test expecting this behavior. \n\nIf power button is used for confirmation, there is no intuitive way for a user to cancel the mode transition without a keyboard. On firmware screens, I think we should do:\n\n* power button short press -\u003e shut down\n* power button long press -\u003e confirmation",
      "parentUuid": "052373c0_faeda4c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 737,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 737,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "d74115262d8693fd8dbc556b553e91c7eed84d36",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
